    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The only runnable test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other files in the package are an abstract base and a helper), and both its tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` behavior for `POST /api/owners` with minimal structural impact by adding small, cohesive units rather than touching the large controller class.\n\n**Changes (4 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an editable `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's accepted on input and returned on output, serialized as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` JPA column plus a simple getter/setter (each CC 1).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added one `@Mapping` annotation on the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` method plus a small `defaultRegistrationDate` helper that returns `LocalDate.now()` when the supplied date is null \u2014 mirroring the existing `normalizeTelephone` pattern.\n\nI deliberately avoided the `addOwner` controller method, which lives in a large class (high WMC_other); the defaulting lives instead in the mapper, a small interface with low surrounding complexity. Result: when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date; a supplied date is preserved; both are returned in ISO format.",
